WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.671
Welcome to Module 4 Aggregating Data with PostgreSQL
In the previous

00:00:05.697 --> 00:00:11.158
module we worked mainly with individual rows Here we
move from detail

00:00:11.184 --> 00:00:16.685
records to summaries that can answer analytical
questions The important

00:00:16.711 --> 00:00:20.685
idea is that aggregation is not only about writing
COUNT SUM or

00:00:20.711 --> 00:00:26.596
AVG Before you calculate anything decide what one
result row should represent

00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:32.783
That is the grain of the summary Throughout this
module you can

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:38.194
run the PostgreSQL examples directly in the browser
On code slides you

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.562
can also use Copy and paste the same query into the
pgAdmin

00:00:41.589 --> 00:00:47.575
Query Tool for additional practice We will build
from simple aggregate functions

00:00:47.602 --> 00:00:52.825
to GROUP BY WHERE and HAVING conditional aggregation
subtotals and window functions

00:00:53.749 --> 00:00:57.196
Keep asking the same question what does one row in
my result

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:57.552
mean
